WEBVTT

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.580
Is this...

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.170
a dream?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.830
Teko!

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.560
You're every bit as cute as I expected!

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.280
This is so embarrassing.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:46.900
What?!

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.800
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.810
This is the only Halloween we get all year. What's the point if you don't cosplay? {## I don't know how I feel about the substitution of 'cosplay' now for just 'being in costume'. people don't care about the roleplay aspect anymore, and it's like it's just replaced the word 'costume' entirely for anything that's from media or the like. tsk, tsk}{speak for yourself re acting}

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.040
It's so mysterious.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:04.710
Everything I see looks like it came straight out of a 
fairy tale or my imagination, so it almost feels like a dream.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.170
But this isn't a dream, right?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.380
What are you doing?

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.440
<i>I'm holding a broom right now!</i>

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:21.580
It really isn't a dream!

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.770
Of course not.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.530
It's real, but feels like a dream.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:29.070
It feels like a dream, but it's real.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.230
Maybe we'll actually fall into a dream at some point without noticing! {## a nice, explicitly undefined time is warranted, else it sounds imminent}

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.990
I wouldn't mind doing that with you.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.870
Then let's get right to exploring this magical dreamscape!

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:47.330
Just for today, this is Marine Town Wonderland!

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:54.240
There's so much I wanted to talk to you about

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:54.240
hanashitakatta koto takusan atta no ni

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.580
But my mind went blank when I saw your face

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.580
kao miru to wasurechau

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:08.190
Every time you peek in to pick me up after school my heart lights up

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:08.190
houkago mukae ni kitekureru no ga ureshikute

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:15.440
I wonder why I so hopelessly feel this way about you

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:15.440
doushite kimi ja nakucha dame na no kana

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.930
It can't be explained with words

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.930
setsumei wa dekinai no

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.390
A surprisingly short while ago, {## 'recent' doesn't operate in this capacity'}

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.140
I wouldn't have had the courage to participate in an event like this. {## I think this better enough that it outweighs mirroring later on, you may disagree}

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.070
Thanks for inviting me, Pikari.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.900
Think nothing of it, and thank you too!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.610
My lovely princess, let us revel in the day's festivities.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.850
I shall be your escort.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:43.690
Very well.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.410
I am in your hands. {## 'fate' is really like they're gonna go fight a monster or something}

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.350
Good, looks like I lost her.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:12.870
My stupid sister forced me into this costume because all the shops give cosplayers half-off. {## I had to listen to the Japanese for this, I thought it was something like all the costumes were half-off at first / I can't deny that cosplay provides a very handy nominal, though / 'charge half-off' is weird, because 'charge' is negative and 'half-off' positive}

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.480
Catch me if you can!

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.400
Kokoro-chan?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:20.320
Pikari-san...

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.760
Way! Too! Cute!

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.570
No, um...

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.960
Pikari, who's this?

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.410
Oh, right, you've never actually met before.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.670
This is Kokoro-chan, the girl I told you about.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.300
<i>So it's her...</i>

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.920
And this is Teko, my classmate from school.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.970
Nice to meet you.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:43.630
You too.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.470
Praise be!

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.720
There are two beautiful princesses before me!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:56.560
Please allow your prince a moment to fetch both of you drinks to quench your thirst! {## not how 'respite' works, not -really- how procure works, not how 'quell' works unless intentionally weird. 'quench' is the normal, 'slake' is really uncommon / i wonder if this should be 'thirsts'}{what is slake}

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.540
She ran off.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:03.740
Yeah.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.880
Those girls are so adorable.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.080
You think they're sisters?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.700
<i>This silence... is awkward.</i>

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:20.630
What drinks do you think she'll get us?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:21.820
Dunno.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:28.300
<i>As the elder, I have to take the lead in conversation! {## subtle diff. between 'have' and 'need. consider 'must' and 'require', respectively, it's that difference. so alt. 'must'}</i>

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.130
Kokoro-chan, you met Pikari at the ocean this summer, didn't you? {## arguable, but better to just dodge the ambiguity}

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.010
Pikari told me.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.350
Yes, several times.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.330
Several?

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.940
Yes, several.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.240
I also ran into her downtown the other day.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.010
We went to see the sakura foliage.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.860
<i>So it was Kokoro-chan she was with that time.</i>

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:56.420
So... what about you, Teko-san?

00:05:56.420 --> 00:06:01.920
Huh?! W-We're in the same class, so I see her basically every day. {## 'nearly' (and also 'almost') are more literal than figurative (cf. 'basically', 'virtually') and this reads as there in truth being days she doesn't see Teko (whether true or not) rather than Teko just hedging her sentence}

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:09.640
Still, going to see the sakura foliage together almost sounds like a date. {## not two sentences, but one sentence with ellipsis looks like 'still going' and not 'still, going', since the comma's overridden}

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.770
Oh, well...

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.100
Yes.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.470
<i>Huh?</i>

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.060
<i>What's that?</i>

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:22.040
<i>She didn't deny it was a... d-date. {## it's so weird seeing mid-sentence stutter like that}</i>

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:28.200
I've gone to see the sakura boulevard with Pikari before too. {she's jelly as fuck}{## wow, this is actually correct usage of 'jealous' for once, good job}

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:31.060
They sure were beautiful in full bloom. {## 'seeing them ... was beautiful' is no, because that means the -experience- was beautiful}

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:40.540
Sorry for the wait!

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.500
Extend your hands, princesses.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.720
Let's go, Pikari.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.680
I... might be lost. {## when did this turn into a harem}

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.120
What's with their unreasonable cuteness?

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:05.820
Huh?

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.410
Advisor Cha?

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:11.160
Pikari?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:17.450
What the... {## even 'What the...'. 'the?' just looks so gross}

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:20.580
Mato-chan-sensei.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.100
So you're the one who brought him.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:27.170
What? No, I came here alone to drink some beer.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.710
Cold beer!

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.170
Huh? Then why...

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:35.470
Don't ask me. In any case, looks like the whole Diving Club is here now. {## it needs this, else it sounds planned}

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.640
The whole club?

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.230
Well, well.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:45.380
Wait, should I say Octo-chan-senpai and Octo-kun-senpai?

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.320
You don't have to correct yourself.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.940
Are you here for the Halloween parade too?

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.980
Nope, for work. {## '[we're here] for work'}

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:55.490
Between the camp and everything else, money's running pretty tight. {## unclear what was running tight before / what is she even referring to? the navigation lesson episode?}

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.720
These costumes are for work! Aren't they cool?

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.260
A man of the sea! {## is not talking to her}

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:04.270
Man?

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.960
What kind of job is it?

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.430
We're supposed to host and promote an event...

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:10.580
What kind?

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.050
Oh, are you interested?

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.930
It's going to start soon.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:18.630
Anyone can participate if they're in costume, and it's a simple borrowing race. {while scavenger hunt is a real term, the difference is that you must borrow something from a person, you can't just buy or find it}{## well, alright}

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.030
Upyo, that sounds like a blast!

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:25.050
Unfortunately, not a single person has signed up.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:29.850
Honestly, don't they want the big prize?

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.370
Big prize?

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:32.860
What's that? {## 'What is the big prize' v. 'What's a "big prize"?'}

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:36.950
The big prize... is right over here!

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:41.790
It's <i>too</i> big!

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:49.140
I cannot deny the theory that it's the prize itself keeping people away.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:50.710
That's definitely a fact.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:54.180
An octopus... So cool... {## octolips at it again}

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:57.510
We might not have any choice but to add an extra prize.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.390
That's true.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.610
An extra prize...

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.600
Like a shoulder massage?

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.350
Or a belly beating!

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:06.850
Maybe a handshake? {## what}

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.460
A celebratory song?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:09.560
A caricature?

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:10.610
A fortune-telling? {## correct}

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.600
Getting to pet Advisor Cha?

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:14.700
Being suckled on by Ohime? {## alt. 'licked', 'sucked on by' / less than ideal, but 'suckled by Ohime' means primarily that -Ohime- is the one providing milk}

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.320
A kiss from the prince!

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.040
I want a kiss from the prince.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.790
If you would be so kind as to enter, my princess, then as your prince...

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.790
Entry

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.250
I would gladly offer my lips.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.850
I'll do it! I'm gonna get the prince's kiss! {## same one}

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:42.180
Mommy, the prince is gonna kiss me! {if my tiny daughter yelled this at me, I'd get worried}

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.350
Pikari!

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.880
This is getting out of control! {## Hanamaru, you've... really let yourself go}

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:00.410
If you would like to participate, 
please take one card and put it in the box!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.770
Ane-chan-senpai!

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:04.120
What now?!

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:05.990
Tekochin?

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.460
You needn't worry.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.420
I shall protect Pikari's lips. {## k-kakkoii}

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:22.140
We will now begin the Borrowing Trick-or-Treating! {when used as a noun, it has hyphens. when used as a phrase, it doesn't}{## that's not what MWebs says, but anyway the nominal is the gerundive (see: Cambridge)}

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.060
Would all participants please gather at the start line?

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.920
The rules are simple!

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.480
This is a borrowing race limited to the surrounding area.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:37.440
All you need to do is make one complete lap around the venue counterclockwise.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:42.920
The item cards picked earlier have been placed face-down randomly on that table. {## 'you' sounds like it's attached to the original person, which isn't (?) the case}

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:45.740
The first card you pick will list your item.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:51.570
As you go around, you'll have to ask bystanders "Give me whatever, or I'll play a trick on you!"

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:56.710
Moreover, you are forbidden from telling others that this is for a borrowing race.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:00.430
You are also forbidden from leaving the venue. {## he repeats it, so why not?}

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:03.460
Pikari, wait for me!

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:07.270
One, two. One, two.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.270
You're playing too, Kokoro-chan?

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.970
Well, I am in costume and everything. I figured I might as well.

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:15.410
<i>I can't lose!</i>

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:20.610
Okay, is everybody ready? {## I know you don't like 'Okay, everyone, are you all ready?' but ditching the first comma is incorrect}{wrong}

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.910
On your marks...

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.710
Get set...

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:28.200
And! {## I feel like you could just leave this one out}

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:30.160
Go!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.710
Best of luck.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.370
Leading the pack are the generic gods. {## 'universal' is weird. alt. nondescript, etc. stuff like that, what does 'universal' even mean?}

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:41.930
But wait! Someone's broken through to the front!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:46.640
Clad in a crimson dress, it's the flowering red rose! {## 'donned' doesn't work this way. 'donning a ...', but suggests that that action just happened}

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:52.270
But hot on her tail is the blooming white lily of the valley! {## ugh. 'floral' is a -really- bad descriptor for a flower; even 'flowery' is better, but I'll leave this to you}

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:55.970
Kokoro-chan is too!

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:56.680
Settle down.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.770
The two dazzling flowers are leading the way! {## this isn't how you use 'blazing', that's for -making- (precisely, -marking-) paths}

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:04.110
What's this?! A monkey has just leapt ahead!

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:07.590
Victory is mine!

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:14.820
L-Lipstick... Any women around here?

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.350
It's do or die! {## jaja-n, for similar reasons when it's an actual verb (see 'kill or be killed') and not a modifier, no hyphens. see: Tennyson: 'theirs but to do and die', like that}

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.550
Trick or lipstick! {because trick or lipstick just doesn't flow as well}{## are you even trying? / but it's impossible to force this for the rest}

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.470
Pervert! {## alt. 'a pervert', I don't like full sentences with these, I'm sure you know}

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.260
I do and died! {## though like, this isn't great either / 'done for'? meaning's different}

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:24.300
Old man beard

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:24.300
Handkerchief

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:26.900
B-Beard?

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:27.930
See ya!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.770
Oh no, there's no time to hesitate!

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:34.240
Get away, you degenerate!

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:35.570
L-Lipstick...

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.410
Thanks.

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.360
A beard!

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:55.120
<i>How could I possibly ask for his beard?!</i>

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:59.590
Easy-peasy! Everyone has a handkerchief! {##Japanesey}

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.500
Cha! Ohime!

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:03.050
Hey!

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.640
Give me a handkerchief, or I'll play a trick on you!

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:13.850
And if I don't give you a handkerchief, what kind of trick will you play? {## yabai}

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:16.980
A topknot...

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:20.200
Give me your hat, or I'll play a trick on you!

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.180
What?

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.590
H-A-T!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.940
R-A-G? {this can honestly be anything as long as the first and last letters change, but since he replys "broom" this is sort of close}{## this is weird as FUCK, when I look at his mouth moving I hear 'hobuki' plain as day, but when I'm looking away I hear 'houki'. It's because his mouth closes when it shouldn't}

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.120
Give me some gloves, or I'll play a trick on you!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.160
You need gloves?

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:36.940
Sure thing. I was just about to start knitting a pair.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:37.580
Huh?!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:40.130
Um, well... Sorry about this.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.590
Give me your bandages, or I'll play a trick on you!

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:50.950
Currently, the goal area is completely silent. {## 'is now' depicts change of state from just earlier}

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:54.480
It seems that everyone's having a tough time.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:01.930
Oh? Katori-sensei, fancy meeting you here. {## I didn't know you'd be here is..., mm, implies an odd expectation}

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.110
Towano-sensei!

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:07.850
It seems that wherever there's beer, there you are.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:09.070
Right back at you.

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:15.900
Drinking at home is all well and good, but spending time out and about at a lively event is nice too.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:16.990
I feel you.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:20.960
And wouldn't you know it, I get to enjoy watching my students have a good time too.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.090
Looks like they're having fun.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.930
Watching them brings back memories.

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:32.390
Of things I left behind long ago.

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:36.560
Just kidding!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.520
Right!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:45.480
That first try was a mistake, but a lady should be fine! {## 'daijoubu' as in 'not a creep' not 'has a handkerchief', since it's the same joke}

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:47.320
Hey!

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:50.160
Give me a handkerchief, or I'll play a trick on you!

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.080
My goodness!

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.660
What kind of trick are you going to play?

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.960
Please play a trick on me! {totally an okama's voice}{## that's a great scream}

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.590
Give me a handkerchief, or I'll play a trick on you!

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:06.090
A trick? Bring it on! {## why did she think this dude would have a handkerchief / there's only one place to store it}

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:15.470
What is this feeling?

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:18.550
It's like I'm being followed.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.730
<i>I have to be brave! {## yeah I don't think this needs to match}</i>

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:32.320
<i>If I don't, then Pikari...</i>

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:33.700
<i>Okay, here I go!</i>

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.750
Um, I'm so sorry!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:52.210
I-If you don't give me your beard, 
I might have to play a trick on you!

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:53.580
What? My beard?

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:56.180
Sure thing, I don't mind.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.280
I-I don't... need... that much...

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:03.720
This is actually just a fake beard.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:06.110
Th-Thank you very much.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.070
<i>Now I can save Pikari!</i>

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:18.490
None of the participants seem to be coming back.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:23.180
Oh, Ohime! I've been looking everywhere for you.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.250
Principal?!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.080
Good afternoon, teachers.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.090
Huh? Is Ohime here alone?

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:33.050
Yeah, but Advisor Cha should soon be... oh?

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:33.050
Here she comes!

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:36.550
It's her!

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.970
The flowering red rose who started strong! {}

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.310
Teko!

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.690
